course: dictionary
lesson: 4103
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are the context. «Sasha's dad's girlfriend paints her nails and takes her shopping.» The clues are dad and shopping, so girlfriend here means a woman who is in a romantic relationship with Sasha's dad.
explain: The same word can mean something different when a girl talks about her friends. «My girlfriends and I are going swimming on Saturday.» Here girlfriends means close female friends. Always ask: who is speaking, and what is the story about? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Be kind when you talk about someone's girlfriend or boyfriend. Teasing someone is not funny if it upsets them, and asking about it as a dare is rude. People's private lives are their own business. If teasing upsets you, tell a grown-up you trust, and they can help.
fact: A girlfriend is a girl or woman that someone is in a romantic relationship with.
fact: A girlfriend can also be a female friend, often said by women about their friends, especially in the USA.
fact: Phrases you may meet include his girlfriend, her girlfriend, my girlfriend and ex-girlfriend.
fact: Boys and girls can be just friends.
fact: Asking someone about their girlfriend or boyfriend as a dare is rude, because people's private lives are not a joke.
exercise: «Sasha's dad's girlfriend takes her shopping.» What does girlfriend mean here? | *A woman in a romantic relationship with Sasha's dad | A shop assistant | A girl who is Sasha's best friend at school
exercise: «My girlfriends and I are going swimming on Saturday.» Said by a girl, what does girlfriends most likely mean? | Teachers at the pool | People who live next door to a shop | *Close female friends
exercise: Ben says, «Asking someone about their girlfriend as a dare is fine.» Is he right? | *No, people's private lives are not a joke | Yes, but only at school | Yes, it is a great game if everyone laughs
test: Which two meanings does girlfriend have? | A teacher, or a school helper | *A romantic partner, or a close female friend | A petrol station, or a kind of shop
test: Which phrase shows a girlfriend who used to be someone's girlfriend? | my girlfriend | her girlfriends | *ex-girlfriend
exam: Ella's teacher says, «Be kind when you talk about someone's girlfriend, and never ask as a dare.» What does she mean? | *Respect people's private lives and be kind | Tease people until they laugh | Ask everyone loudly in class about their private lives
